00:42:26.400 --> 00:42:27.420
So first and foremost,

00:42:27.420 --> 00:42:28.470
it's really been a pleasure

00:42:28.470 --> 00:42:30.043
just to hear the perspective

00:42:30.043 --> 00:42:32.940
of so many different distinguished faculty

00:42:32.940 --> 00:42:35.790
and to to be in conversation with you all.

00:42:35.790 --> 00:42:39.419
So I think that the conversation
that we're having here

00:42:39.419 --> 00:42:42.840
and around the country about ChatGPT is

00:42:42.840 --> 00:42:46.230
really both a challenge and an opportunity

00:42:46.230 --> 00:42:48.540
to think deeper and more critically

00:42:48.540 --> 00:42:50.539
about what we do at the university

00:42:50.539 --> 00:42:54.667
as students and as educators, and why,

00:42:55.917 --> 00:42:57.330
and it's definitely true

00:42:57.330 --> 00:43:01.140
that concerns about academic
dishonesty are warranted,

00:43:01.140 --> 00:43:05.017
but ultimately we do what
we do here as students,

00:43:05.017 --> 00:43:07.767
not just to gain credentials

00:43:07.767 --> 00:43:11.310
or to get a grade on a transcript,

00:43:11.310 --> 00:43:15.030
but really to learn how to think, to read,

00:43:15.030 --> 00:43:18.420
and to solve problems after we leave Yale,

00:43:18.420 --> 00:43:22.020
and so borrowing from what
Professor Wexler said earlier,

00:43:22.020 --> 00:43:24.600
striving for the reality of learning,

00:43:24.600 --> 00:43:26.088
rather than just its appearance is

00:43:26.088 --> 00:43:28.020
really what matters to me,

00:43:28.020 --> 00:43:30.600
and I think a lot of my peers would agree.

00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:32.165
So I think, with that in mind,

00:43:32.165 --> 00:43:35.040
the critical work is to figure out

00:43:35.040 --> 00:43:38.640
how to responsibly engage
with the technology as a tool,

00:43:38.640 --> 00:43:40.306
rather than a crutch,

00:43:40.306 --> 00:43:41.760
because tech is

00:43:41.760 --> 00:43:44.580
really an increasingly
important part of the world

00:43:44.580 --> 00:43:45.413
that we live in,

00:43:45.413 --> 00:43:46.680
and our everyday lives,

00:43:46.680 --> 00:43:49.110
especially, as a 21st century student,

00:43:49.110 --> 00:43:50.730
I feel they need to know

00:43:50.730 --> 00:43:54.600
how to engage with this kind
of technology responsibly

00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:57.960
and understand it's
limits and it's biases,

00:43:57.960 --> 00:44:01.038
which Professor Vishnoi spoke to earlier.

00:44:01.038 --> 00:44:03.322
Some faculty at other universities

00:44:03.322 --> 00:44:05.940
have proposed using ChatGPT

00:44:05.940 --> 00:44:08.640
to represent one side of
a debate for instance,

00:44:08.640 --> 00:44:10.699
and then having students
dialogue with that.

00:44:10.699 --> 00:44:13.620
So I still believe that
there's room for us

00:44:13.620 --> 00:44:16.291
to engage with this
responsibly in the classroom

00:44:16.291 --> 00:44:18.720
while still maintaining the development

00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:21.210
of those critical thinking skills

00:44:21.210 --> 00:44:25.830
that technology alone
shouldn't take the place of,

00:44:25.830 --> 00:44:26.910
but all in all,

00:44:26.910 --> 00:44:29.910
I'm really excited about the changes

00:44:29.910 --> 00:44:32.910
that our engagement with
ChatGPT will inspire.

00:44:32.910 --> 00:44:37.084
So rethinking how we understand
learning and evaluation,

00:44:37.084 --> 00:44:38.624
creating more opportunities

00:44:38.624 --> 00:44:42.538
for experiential learning
and problem-based learning.

00:44:42.538 --> 00:44:46.290
So, ultimately, I think staying true

00:44:46.290 --> 00:44:49.020
to our broader mission of learning

00:44:49.020 --> 00:44:51.000
and receiving an education

00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:53.790
to go out into the
world and solve problems

00:44:53.790 --> 00:44:55.650
should remain at the heart of what we do,

00:44:55.650 --> 00:44:57.925
but really the opportunity here is,

00:44:57.925 --> 00:45:00.600
to learn how to work with the technology,

00:45:00.600 --> 00:45:02.790
understand what it can't do,

00:45:02.790 --> 00:45:05.430
and build those critical skills

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:07.876
and creativity that we'll need

00:45:07.876 --> 00:45:11.703
to take with us once we
leave the university.

00:45:15.240 --> 00:45:16.780
